.TH CAMELION++ 1 "November 2026" "Camelion++ 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
camelion++ \- Notepad++-style source code editor for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B camelion++
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR[:\fIline\fR[:\fIcol\fR]] ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Camelion++ is a tabbed source code editor built on Scintilla and Lexilla.
It reads Notepad++ configuration files (langs.xml, stylers.xml, themes,
autoCompletion and functionList definitions) and loads Linux plugins
through a Notepad++-compatible plugin interface. Plugins can be installed
from a signed nppPluginList with Plugins > Plugins Admin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-n line
Go to \fIline\fR.
.TP
.BI \-c column
Go to \fIcolumn\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l language
Open the files with the given language, e.g. \fB\-lpython\fR.
.TP
.B \-ro
Open the files read-only.
.TP
.B \-nosession
Neither restore nor save the session.
.TP
.B \-noPlugin
Do not load any plugin.
.TP
.B \-multiInst
Start a new instance instead of reusing the running one.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-pluginlist
Print the status of the plugin list (source, signature, entries) and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/camelion++/
config.xml, session.xml, optional langs.xml / stylers.xml, themes/, plugins/Config/
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/camelion++/plugins/
Plugins installed by the user (\fIName\fR/\fIName\fR.so).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/camelion++/plugins/
System-wide plugins and Config/nppPluginList.so.
.SH LICENSE
GPL-3.0-or-later.
